---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PHONE, PHONE_TEL } from '../../lib/site.ts';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How it works"
  description="How Foundation Repair Advocate works: floor plan scan, scheduled visit, floor elevation survey, written report, optional 12-month resurvey — Arizona."
>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">How it works</h1>
    <p class="lead">Simple process. No pressure. You know the fee before we drive.</p>

    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Call or text</strong>
        Tell us what you're seeing — cracks, doors, an estimate you don't trust, or just worry.
        We'll decide if a survey makes sense and quote the visit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Floor plan before we arrive</strong>
        We send simple instructions for a phone-based floor plan scan (CubiCasa or similar). You walk
        the house once; we import the plan so Distress and elevation work align on site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>On-site visit</strong>
        Floor elevation survey of accessible floors, walkthrough, photos as needed, and a straight
        conversation — usually a few hours on site depending on size.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Report &amp; watch list</strong>
        Contour map, plain-language summary, what to monitor, and questions for any repair
        contractors you invite later. Delivered quickly — often within days.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Optional: resurvey in ~12 months</strong>
        If we recommend monitoring, we can return and compare — movement documented, not guessed.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <section>
      <h2>Already have paperwork?</h2>
      <p>
        Bring the other company's estimate, floor survey, or photos. Second-opinion reviews start
        from what you already paid for — we add independent measurement and context.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>During repair (optional)</h2>
      <p>
        Some homeowners want an advocate on site while piers go in — not to direct the crew, but to
        ask questions, compare work to the bid, and keep paperwork straight. Ask us if that's
        appropriate for your job.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="contact-box">
      <p><strong>Start here:</strong></p>
      <a class="phone-link" href={`tel:${PHONE_TEL}`}>{PHONE}</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
